        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#eef4fb;font-family:system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#182d4c'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:6px solid #294b83;border-bottom:1px solid #182d4c;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>PRIMITIVE · edge-class</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:850 clamp(36px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.035em;text-wrap:balance;color:#182d4c'>Edge Class</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.4 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#46617f'>The definition of a kind of relationship: what it means and where it may connect.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Meaning</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>An Edge Class is the kind of a relationship, written as a graph of its own. It says what the relationship means, which kinds of node may sit at each end, and how an edge of that kind is drawn. An edge points to its class by its type; the class is not one of the edges it describes.</p></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #182d4c'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#182d4c'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #a6bed9'><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #a6bed9;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#46617f'>Encoded as</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#182d4c;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>an authored graph consumed as an edge-class resource; distinct from an Edge instance</dd></dl></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Invariants</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Connection rules have one shared reader. Styling does not grant connection legality. A class graph is not itself one of the relationship instances it describes.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Contract</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A class decides three things. Meaning: a sentence an author can read. Legality: <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>sourceKinds</code> and <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>targetKinds</code> (empty or <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>any</code> permits all) and <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>maxOutgoing</code> or <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>maxIncoming</code>, stated only where the limit is true of the relationship everywhere. Appearance: its Strokes, which change how an edge looks and never what it means. How many connections a particular Port takes is declared on the Port (<code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>metadata.repeatable</code>), not on the class.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>edgeClassRule reads key, sourceKinds, targetKinds, maxOutgoing and maxIncoming. Empty kind lists or any permit all kinds; absent limits are unbounded. Numeric limits are nonnegative integer bounds. Classes also carry presentation/stroke information read by edgeClass.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Ports and Relationships</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The class constrains relationship endpoints by semantic kinds and cardinality. A <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>surface</code> edge connects a root to its first face; <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>next-face</code> connects a face to the next face or to the terminal Glyph.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Behavior</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>edgeClassRegistry loads the default collection; deriveEdgeClassFromGraphPayload derives each rule. The editor and validator share edgeLegality. Core classes live in the content repository, so changing runtime code alone cannot publish a new class rule.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>To make a class, open the Edge Class Template, set its key and label, write what it means, set the kinds at each end, style its Strokes, and save. An edge whose type is that key is then checked against the rule: the editor refuses a connection the class does not allow, and a graph that already has one is warned about when it loads.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Known gaps</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Load order and remote publication are deployment concerns. Tests loading local class graphs verify local contracts, not that the remote collection has been deployed.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Representations</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>A class is a graph: a Property for each rule and render setting, and a Stroke node for each paint layer. A Stroke paints because it is in the graph, not because anything connects it; a stroke that should not paint is disabled.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Not the Edge instance, not a node-class binding, and not an inference from an edge’s color or label.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Examples</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The linked example is a separate graph. Inspect its relevant nodes and relationships; this specification does not embed or execute the example.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>The <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>leads-to</code> class says one thing follows from another, and joins any source to any target. The <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>invokes</code> class ends only at a Method. The Surface Edge Class states its meaning, its kinds and its limits as Properties, and its paint as Strokes.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#294b83'>Where this lives</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Source (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/edgeClass.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/edgeClassRegistry.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/edgeLegality.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/portCapacity.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>Focused tests (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/coreEdgeClasses.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/edgeLegality.test.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#dce9f7;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/portCapacity.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;color:#253c58'>These pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='primary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:12px;border-top:3px solid #294b83'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:750 26px/1.1 system-ui;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#182d4c'>Surface</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#46617f'>A worked example: classes/edges/surface.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/edges/surface/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#294b83'>Open the example →</a></section></div></div></div></div></div>"
        },
