      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Meaning",
        "body": "An Edge Class is the kind of a relationship, written as a graph of its own. It says what the relationship means, which kinds of node may sit at each end, and how an edge of that kind is drawn. An edge points to its class by its type; the class is not one of the edges it describes.",
