    {
      "id": "edge-class-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 450,
        "y": -250
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "A class decides three things. Meaning: a sentence an author can read. Legality: `sourceKinds` and `targetKinds` (empty or `any` permits all) and `maxOutgoing` or `maxIncoming`, stated only where the limit is true of the relationship everywhere. Appearance: its Strokes, which change how an edge looks and never what it means. How many connections a particular Port takes is declared on the Port (`metadata.repeatable`), not on the class.\n\nedgeClassRule reads key, sourceKinds, targetKinds, maxOutgoing and maxIncoming. Empty kind lists or any permit all kinds; absent limits are unbounded. Numeric limits are nonnegative integer bounds. Classes also carry presentation/stroke information read by edgeClass.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592057003,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-edge-class"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
