    {
      "id": "edge-class-behavior",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Behavior",
      "position": {
        "x": 2130,
        "y": -250
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Behavior",
        "body": "edgeClassRegistry loads the default collection; deriveEdgeClassFromGraphPayload derives each rule. The editor and validator share edgeLegality. Core classes live in the content repository, so changing runtime code alone cannot publish a new class rule.\n\nTo make a class, open the Edge Class Template, set its key and label, write what it means, set the kinds at each end, style its Strokes, and save. An edge whose type is that key is then checked against the rule: the editor refuses a connection the class does not allow, and a graph that already has one is warned about when it loads.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592057005,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
